<content>
  <section><title>Cool Down (5 minutes)</title>
<title>Student Activity</title>
<list class="os-raise-noindent" type="enumerated">
  <item>The line in each shaded graph represents \( y=2x \). Which graph including the shaded region represents \( y&gt;2x \)? </item>
</list>
<list type="enumerated">
  <item><media><image alt="Graph of an inequality." src="https://k12.openstax.org/contents/raise/resources/f56d9084ccc1d977e9f9f131674dc98701e1c603"/> </media></item>
  <item><media><image alt="Graph of an inequality." src="https://k12.openstax.org/contents/raise/resources/ffce4b4ce392c6b05fdf0abf32d6ccdb27ee54c7"/> </media></item>
  <item><media><image alt="Graph of an inequality." src="https://k12.openstax.org/contents/raise/resources/540b2a3955081c4ac51decba8e8bd8849d7aa077"/> </media></item>
  <item><media><image alt="Graph of an inequality." src="https://k12.openstax.org/contents/raise/resources/311fba5d50594deb7b414e6a72709925e8ac0d8d"/></media></item>
</list>
<para><emphasis>Answer:</emphasis> Graph C</para>
<list start="2" type="enumerated">
  <item>Explain your reasons for choosing that graph.</item>
</list>
<para><emphasis>Answer:</emphasis></para>
  <para>Compare your answer: Your answer may vary, but here is a sample. </para>
<title>Response to Student Thinking</title>
<title>More Chances</title>
<para>Activities 2.11.2 and 2.11.3 both provide additional opportunities to consider how to make decisions about which side of the boundary line to shade.</para></section>
</content>
